 "Initiate their leadership ePortfolio, which will be used throughout the minor.", "Apply basic leadership skills of conflict resolution, ethics, appreciating diversity, working effectively in teams."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2755, "crseId": 364483, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LEAD", "catalogNbr": "3100", "titleShort": "Foundations in Leadership", "titleLong": "Foundations in Leadership: Skills for Professional Success and Life", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 4245, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "04:25PM", "startDt": "01/21/2020", "endDt": "05/05/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ljv4", "firstName": "Larry", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Van De Valk"}], "pattern": "R", "facilityDescr": "Warren Hall B73", "bldgDescr": "Warren Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "WRNB73", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Preference given to students in the Leadership Minor."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/21/2020", "endDt": "05/12/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "HY", "instrModeDescrshort": "HY-OLIP", "instrModeDescr": "Hybrid - Online & In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "SUI", "gradingBasisShort": "S/U NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/21/2020", "sessionEndDt": "05/12/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This course frames leadership as a particular way of approaching life, one that is essential to both personal fulfillment and career effectiveness. The course begins with the inner work of a leader's personal development and then explores how leaders work through others to enhance their influence.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(KCM-AG, SBA-AG)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: 30 students. Enrollment preference given to: Leadership minor students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Develop a critical understanding of contemporary leadership theories, styles, approaches and roles.", "Examine and clarify personal inspirations, values, and purposes in careers and life.", "Learn to align those inner motivations with personal actions, decisions, and communications in order to become more authentic, effective, and influential.", "Build skills for communicating effectively, especially in difficult conversations such as delivering feedback, resolving conflict, and influencing others.", "Practice skills for building effective teams and leading group planning, decision making and problem solving processes.", "Create a personal learning plan and leadership portfolio for supporting personal development.", "Establish a habit of reflection to promote continuous learning and effective leadership."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2755, "crseId": 369495, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "LEAD", "catalogNbr": "4925", "titleShort": "Leadership Minor ePortfolio", "titleLong": "Leadership Minor ePortfolio", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttr